{"id":"effect-ad94fe2a-1f3e-58d8-a64d-e9a7a251b94e","sessionId":"b5ba4547-ee1f-8315-0462-bca51b9ff125","turnId":"turn-6cc49f01a763b1f62398ae61c5b7189c","inputEntryId":"user-turn-6cc49f01a763b1f62398ae61c5b7189c-1","createdAt":1794279550379,"updatedAt":1794279550390,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading ANSWER.md","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","offset":null,"limit":2000}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"38 lines from ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-KfD384/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for System Prompt Caching Issue\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the entire system prompt to be re-cached, making subsequent calls pay full price for the static instructions. This happened because `build_system()` concatenated the static INSTRUCTIONS with the dynamic athlete context into a single cacheable block. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, causing a cache miss.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate cacheable blocks:\n1. Static INSTRUCTIONS (never changes)\n2. Dynamic athlete context (changes with facts)\n\nThis way, when `save_fact` updates the athlete context, only the dynamic block is re-cached, while the static INSTRUCTIONS block remains cached and can be reused across all calls.\n\n## Change Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # Split into separate cacheable blocks: static instructions and dynamic athlete context.\n    # This way, save_fact (which only changes athlete context) doesn't evict the static instructions from cache.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\n## Impact\n- The static INSTRUCTIONS (~1024-1046 tokens) will now be cached once and reused across all messages\n- Only the athlete context (~20-80 tokens depending on facts) will be re-cached when facts change\n- This significantly reduces token usage for subsequent calls after a `save_fact` operation\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"requestedOffset":null,"requestedLimit":2000,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":false},"durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","approvalSource":"bypass"}}
{"id":"assistant-95abcc04-c6dd-5e59-aefc-cc9d2645ff1d","sessionId":"b5ba4547-ee1f-8315-0462-bca51b9ff125","turnId":"turn-6cc49f01a763b1f62398ae61c5b7189c","inputEntryId":"user-turn-6cc49f01a763b1f62398ae61c5b7189c-1","createdAt":1794279586484,"updatedAt":1794279586484,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Everything is complete. Let me create a final summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. The problem was that the system prompt was being built as a single cacheable block that combined both static instructions and dynamic athlete context. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, causing a cache miss and forcing subsequent calls to pay full price for the static instructions.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified the `build_system()` function in `bot.py` to split the system prompt into two separate cacheable blocks:\n1. Static INSTRUCTIONS (never changes)\n2. Dynamic athlete context (changes with facts)\n\nThis way, when `save_fact` updates the athlete context, only the dynamic block needs re-caching, while the static INSTRUCTIONS block remains cached and reusable across all calls.\n\n**Files Changed:**\n- `bot.py` - Modified the `build_system()` function (lines 128-136)\n- `ANSWER.md` - Created documentation of the fix\n\nThe change is minimal, focused, and has been verified to work correctly through testing. The static instructions (~1024-1046 tokens) will now be cached once and reused, while only the athlete context (~20-80 tokens) will be re-cached when facts change, significantly reducing token usage for subsequent calls after a `save_fact` operation."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
